  "statuteText": "656:33 Official Absence, Religious Observance, and Disability Absentee Ballots. –\n\nPrior to any state election, the secretary of state shall prepare, in such quantity as the secretary of state may deem necessary, absence, religious observance, and disability absentee ballots in the same form as nearly as practicable as the official ballot to be used at said election. Said absentee ballots shall have the words \"absentee ballot\" printed on them and shall be similarly endorsed and printed on paper of the same color as that used for official ballots."
